        <p>WARRINGTON MUSICAL SOCIETY THIRD SUBSCRIPTION CONCERT, PARR HALL, ON TUESDAY, FEBRUARY 28111. MIS.CELLANEOUB PROGRAMME. AUGMENTED ORCHESTRA, MENDELSSOHN'S LORBLEY " (SOPRANO Soto: MRS. A. BOOT'). TSuHAIKOWSKI'S " CASSE NOIIETTIS " SUITE. WAGNER'S MARCH ec CHORUS FROM "TANNHAUSER," SEXTET FROM "LUCIA DI LAMMERSIOOIt.” QUINTET FROM " MERRIE ENGLAND," QUARTET FROM " THE YEOMEN OF THE GUARD." By the following Members of the Society SOPRANOS: CONTRALTOS: MRS. A. BOOTH MISS E. D. JEANS Miss G. PEMBERTON Miss M. MIMI:KAU Miss A. DAUNT Mlss M. W. COLLIN TENORS: BASSES : MR. J. RABBITT MR. W. H. WALLINGTON MR J. H. DRAPER MR: J. e 7. BIBBY MR. J. B. HANNAN MR. F. FIELDMOUSE SOLO VIOLIN: MR. ALFRED ROSS. CHORUS AND ORCHESTRA or OVER 20) PERFORM HRS. CONDUCTOR: MR. F. W. CROSSLEY. HON. ORGANIST: MR. W. H. PATToN, MITS. BAC., LEADER OF ORCHESTRA: MR. R. H. PEARSON. PRICES OF ADMISSION :—Reserved Dress Seats. 60. -.1..e",r",ed Centre Gallery and Second Reserved Seats Body of ~ 04. Reserved Side Galleries, 21. ; Unreserved Back "'""erY, Is. (id.; Back Seats (Body of Hall),and Promenade Is Doors open 7.15 p.m Concert 7.45 p m Carriages 10.15 p.m Ticket-holders admitted by early door at 7.0 p.m. The PLAN OF RESERVED SEATS will be opened at Messrs. R. H. I. EARSON'S Ltd.. Bold street, to Subscribers on SATURDAY NEXT, FEBRUARY 18th, and to the general public on and after the following WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 22nd. L. W. REYNOLDS, Hon. Treasurer.</p>
