      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>TO-DAY'S RECIPE.</head>
        <p>TO-DAY'S RECIPE.</p>
        <p>FOILETS OF SOLE A LA MARIE. —Trim the fillets of a pair of medium-sized soles, season them with salt and pepper, and spread the smooth side with two tablespoonfuls of shrimps that are pounded with 2oz. of butter, 2oz. of panada, and the yolks of two eggs, and then rubbed through a wire sieve. Roll the fillets tightly, put three or four on a skewer, with a space between each, dip them in flour, then in beaten egg and breadcrumbs, and fry them by immersing them in hot lard. Dish the fillets in a circle, and garnish the centre with the following: Cut four fillets of sole into pieces 2in. tlo , sub-divide these into fine :strips, lengthways, 4 e them in plenty of flour, put them in a wire ket, and plunge them into hot, clean lard foe 1001 It three minutes; drain them, and season the' with salt and pepper. Serve tartar Sauce separately,</p>
      </div>
