      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0044" n="art0044">
        <head>REMEDY FOR INFLUENZA.</head>
        <p>THE REMEDY FOR INFLUENZA.</p>
        <p>Do you suffer from chills, alternating with sudden gushes, severe headache, accotupanied by difficulty of breathing and symptoms of catarrh, pains in the chest, under and between the shoulders, and a stiffness and soreness of the muscles, loss of appetite and nervous- ness, or are you oppressed with gloomy forebodings and depressed spirits? If you suffer from any of these symptoms, know that they are the forerunners of Influenza, and it behoves you to resort at once to an effective and suitable remedy. It has been established beyond doubt that Quinine is the only specific, and it is clearly demonstrated, that the best way to exhibit Quinine is in the form of GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BirrEns. Each tablespoonful of this preparation contains a full dose of Quinine, combined with the active principles of the well-known remedial agents,—Sarsaparilla, Saffron, , Lavender, Gentian, Burdock and Dandelion, scientifi- cally prepared and mixed in such happy proportions as to form a Tonic Bitters positively unequalled. We can strongly and confidently recommend this preparation, as lit has treated severe cases of Influenza, heavy colds, I extreme weakness of langour, with greater success than any other known remedy. After an attack of inflaenza, patients everywhere admit that they feel more de- pressed and miserable, than while under its influence, and more than they feel after an attack of any other illness. A few doses of GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BITTERS, taken in time, will drive away the sense of extreme helplessness, and will strengthen and fortify those parts which have been weakened by disease, will II brace up the nerves, will purify the blood, and will remove all obstruction and impurities in the human body.</p>
