        <p>WARRINGTON CUP. SEMI-FINAL TIES. SUTTON COMMERCIAL V. LYMM.</p>
        <p>Before a large attendance this match was played on Walker's Brewery ground, Warrington, on Saturday. The interval arrived with the score one goal each. Re- starting, Sutton pressed, and were bombarding the Lymm goal until Eaton cleared. Sutton were now having the better of the play, and from a scrimmage in the goalmouth the ball was rushed through, Sutton thus gaining the lead 25 minutesafter the re-start. W. Sutton got going for Lyrnm, and put in a grand centre, Joe Leah sending in a lightning shot, which struck the cross-bar and rebounded into play. After this Sutton had most of the game, but no further score resulted, and Sutton won a hard-fought game by two goals to one.N3</p>
