        <p>Once in a game with Bateman I left the balls in the seemingly safe position shown on Diagram 60. Bateman's ball was only about a quarter of an inch from the red, and no in-oft` was on into any pocket. Owing to his ball being so far out into the table a masse cannon was practically impossible. No stroke seemed at all on, amd least of all a run-through cannon,; and yet Bateman Played, and made a cannon by an abso- lutely-fair and clean run-through stroke, and be- fore he sat down again the full break had amounted to 181. Afterwards Bateman was kind enough to play the stroke a dozen times, and lo made the cannon eight or nine times. DIAGRAM 61. • • • o Ltd Wa• u. •J r C.••• J J • • Le run-through cau.x.h.L Wll</p>
