        <p>_ BILLIARDS. ---- IsT v.n. (P.W.V.) SOUTH LANCASHIRE REoImENT. —Played at the Sergeants Mess Drill Hall. ST. CLEMENTS IST. SERGEANTS. J. VVolfend en lOO Sergeant Allardice H. Broadhurst W. Holmes 79 Sergeant Potter E. Jones 52 Sergeant Wilcock lOO P. H. Simkin lOO Sergeant Russell H. C. Rhoden 99 Sergeant Ingram lo' 530 Played at St. Clements Club. ST. CLEMENTS Ism SERGEANTS 2ND. W. Carter IJ. Fleming B7 Sergeant Fern T. High= 69 Sergeant Bebbington P A. Evans lOO Sergeant Cliffe 4 Pattison P. Hankinson MEI 523 Win for St. Clements 2nd by 4. ------ Building Students at Messrs. Crosfield' Works. ; The members of the Technical Institute Buildii Students' Association visited the works of Messr Crosfield, Limited, Bank Quay, on Saturday, the firn having kindly granted permission. The party, I 'limbering about 40, were met by Dr. Markel (manag in director), Mr. Lord, Mr. Newall (chief engineer), lama Mr. Burlton (assistant engineer), and first takeo • into the drawing office and shown the drawings of the buildings in progress and those in contemplation, the !latter showing that many important schemes are in view. The buildings in progress of erection and the various departments of the works were visited, evei thing being explained in detail by the guides. One was struck by the elaborate arrangements made to resist fire. The buildings are constructed of the best fire-resisting material, and the firm have an exceltent fire brigade and full appliances of the best and most modern type. For twa and a half hours the party were busy going from one department to another and I were greatly impressed with the really admirable. arrangements in every respect. Afterwards an excel- lent tea was served in the Works' Asembly Roome I A vote of thanks was accorded to Dr. Markel and th, other officials on the proposition • of Mr. Robson seconded Mr. H. 0. Armstrong. In reply, Dr ; Markel saiu that anything which tended to help oo the work of the Technical Institute would alWa3-s hael, his warmest support. Arrangements for the visit had been made by 31r. Newell, jun., and Nr. Spensley.</p>
