        <p>Ison had saved well from a forward rush, Jordan took a pass• and forced his way over cleverly and scored at the corner. At half-time the score read five points tonil in Warrington's favour. After the interval Davies broke icleverly away, but he received little support. Knight after running through the opposition, gave to Harris, that player recording the second try of the afternoon. The visito s pressed hard, only to be repulsed by Berry and Knight and eventually Harris scored after a strong run. Forster next registered a try and then an excellent bout of passing resulted in Runcorn scoring, and a goal being kicked from the try In the last few minutes of the game..Dickenson scored Final score: Warrington, one goal five tries (17 points) ; Runcorn one goal one try (live points). -- LEAGUE (SECOND DIVISION.) - RESULTS AT A GLANCE. _ Pts. Pts. *Barrow *Pontefract • 18 Lancaster 0 Rochdale Hornets 8 *Huddersfield *Dewsbury 6 York *Keighley . RESULTS TO DATE. For. Against. P. W. L. D. G. T. Pts. G. T. P. P. Barrow... 19...17... 2... 0...18 43-165... 7 11— 47... 34 York 2O .16... 2... 2...26 44-184... 7 9 41... 34 Dewsb'ry 17...13... 2... 2...21 37-153... 5 10— 40... 28 H'field K eighley 20...10... 8... 2...31 40-182...11 16-- 70... 22 Pon.',fract 19... 9... 9... 1...32 22-130...17 26-112... 19 R'hdlell. 19... 8... 8... 3...15 22 96...18 21— 99... 19 Castl'fo'd 21... 8...10... 3..32 16— 72...26 27-133... 19 Norm'ton 19... 8...11... 0...14 20— 88...25 26-128... 16 Millom 19... 8...11... 0...12 18— 78...20 36-148... 16 B'gh'se R 20... 5...14... 1...13 18— 80...21 29-129... 11 Lancaster 17... 4...12... 1...10 13— 59...25 38-164... 9 Bramley 18... 3...13... 2...11 10— 52...21 28-126... 8 M'ectimbe 18... 3...15... 0... 8 10— 46...37 58-248... 6</p>
