        <p>prove equal to the occasion. The twelve are : Knight ; Harris, Dickenson, Berry, and Jordan; J. Davies and W. Bate, Coleman, Harmer, 'Foster, Lunt, and Morrison, forwards. Last Saturday, Runcorn "A " were easily defeated by 17 points to 5, Harris getting two and 'Dickenson one of the tries. He showed a good deal of his old pace and dash, but Dickenson was not at his best. 'He will have a sterner task to-day and should be quite at home. The threequarter line is exceeding[y strong and ought to have no difficulty in surprising the Oldharners. The South-West Lancashire League table up-to-date is as follows For. Against. P. W. L. D. G. T. P. G. T. P. Pts. W'gton 7... 5... 1... 1...11 8— 46... 33 15... 11 I Leigh I Wigan 7.. 5 . 2 . 0.. 8 13— 55... 7 5 29... 10 ISt. Helens 7... 2... 4... 1... 4 8— 32... 6 11— 45... 5 Widnes Runcorn 5... 0... 5... 0... 3 5 21... 6 11— 45... 0 If Warrington can manage to win at Wigan next week they will he favourities for the cup once more. 11 I should like to remind my readers that they will ' have an opportunity of being generous to-day to one of the Club's best playing members, viz. : F. Shugars. A collection is to be taken on the ground in his behalf , with the idea of compensating him to some extent for the recent robbery by which he lost -C25. • Hockey. Stockton Heath travelled to Alderley Edge last week with a scratch team which was weakened by one of the eleven arriving at the station just in time to see the . train go out. The Ald.erley ground, although having nice smooth surface, has a peculiar slops up to one of the goals, and this formation is certainly in favour of the home side. Then again the ground has been heavily top-dressed, and on Saturday after the rain, it was little better than playing on a sandy beach.</p>
